{"Non-atomic match_count increment loses counts under concurrency - record.match_count += 1 reads the value in Ruby, increments in memory, then saves, causing two concurrent requests to overwrite each other's count. Should use update_column or SQL increment instead.": 0.9115915894508362, "Only dots are escaped in domain setting - email_in_restriction_setting? uses setting.gsub('.', '\\.') which only escapes dots. Regex metacharacters like +, (, [, or ? in admin-entered domains will cause RegexpError or match unintended patterns. Should use Regexp.escape on each domain segment.": 0.7015589475631714}